{"assets":[],"contentKind":"statement","contestId":"450","diagnostics":[],"document":{"children":[{"attrs":{"level":1,"role":"title"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"A. Jzzhu and Children"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"time_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"time limit per test"},{"kind":"text","text":":"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"1 second"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"memory_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"memory limit per test"},{"kind":"text","text":":"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"256 megabytes"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"body"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"There are "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"n"},{"kind":"text","text":" children in Jzzhu's school. Jzzhu is going to give some candies to them. Let's number all the children from "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"1"},{"kind":"text","text":" to "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"n"},{"kind":"text","text":". The "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"i"},{"kind":"text","text":"-th child wants to get at least "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"ai"},{"kind":"text","text":" candies."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Jzzhu asks children to line up. Initially, the "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"i"},{"kind":"text","text":"-th child stands at the "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"i"},{"kind":"text","text":"-th place of the line. Then Jzzhu start distribution of the candies. He follows the algorithm:"}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"attrs":{"ordered":true},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" Give "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"m"},{"kind":"text","text":" candies to the first child of the line. "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" If this child still haven't got enough candies, then the child goes to the end of the line, else the child go home. "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" Repeat the first two steps while the line is not empty. "}],"kind":"list_item"}],"kind":"list"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Consider all the children in the order they go home. Jzzhu wants to know, which child will be the last in this order?"}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"input_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The first line contains two integers "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"n, m"},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"(1 ≤ n ≤ 100; 1 ≤ m ≤ 100)"},{"kind":"text","text":". The second line contains "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"n"},{"kind":"text","text":" integers "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"a1, a2, ..., an"},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"(1 ≤ ai ≤ 100)"},{"kind":"text","text":"."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"output_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output a single integer, representing the number of the last child."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"samples"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Examples"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"5 2\n1 3 1 4 2\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"4\n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"6 4\n1 1 2 2 3 3\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"6\n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"note"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Note"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Let's consider the first sample. "}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Firstly child 1 gets 2 candies and go home. Then child 2 gets 2 candies and go to the end of the line. Currently the line looks like [3, 4, 5, 2] (indices of the children in order of the line). Then child 3 gets 2 candies and go home, and then child 4 gets 2 candies and goes to the end of the line. Currently the line looks like [5, 2, 4]. Then child 5 gets 2 candies and goes home. Then child 2 gets two candies and goes home, and finally child 4 gets 2 candies and goes home."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Child 4 is the last one who goes home."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"document"},"index":"A","problemCode":"450A","schema":2,"sourceKind":"html","sourceUrl":"https://codeforces.com/contest/450/problem/A"}